afk: reviews dispatch the bundled `reviewer` agent; no worktrees.

Motivation: omp ships a read-only `reviewer` agent (pinned top-tier
model, structured findings output) — "general-purpose subagent" and
manual model choices do not map. Reviewers must never create git
worktrees (phantom state in a jj-colocated repo); read-only git
plumbing covers inspecting other revisions, and parked task refs are
invisible to jj, so git — not jj — is the review interface.

What must survive a rebase:
- Dispatch headers say "agent: reviewer" (no model placeholder).
- Read-only section: git show/diff/log only; `git show [SHA]:path` for
  files at other revisions; never create worktrees, never move HEAD.

